Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the existing patterns. Let me design the complete oRPC API router architecture for the survey platform.

---

## oRPC API Router Design for Survey Platform

Based on my analysis of the existing codebase patterns, here is the complete design for the survey API routers.

### 1. Router Architecture Overview

```
appRouter
├── healthCheck (public)
├── privateData (protected)
├── todo (existing)
├── survey (protected)         # Survey CRUD operations
├── question (protected)       # Question CRUD operations
├── logicRule (protected)      # Logic rule CRUD operations
└── response (mixed)           # Response submission (public) + management (protected)
```

### 2. Database Schema Requirements

Before implementing the routers, the following schema files need to be created in `packages/db/src/schema/`:

#### `/packages/db/src/schema/survey.ts`

```typescript
import { relations } from "drizzle-orm";
import {
	boolean,
	index,
	integer,
	pgTable,
	serial,
	text,
	timestamp,
	varchar,
} from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

import { user } from "./auth";

export const surveyStatus = ["draft", "published", "closed"] as const;
export type SurveyStatus = (typeof surveyStatus)[number];

export const survey = pgTable(
	"survey",
	{
		id: serial("id").primaryKey(),
		title: varchar("title", { length: 255 }).notNull(),
		description: text("description"),
		status: varchar("status", { length: 20 })
			.default("draft")
			.notNull()
			.$type<SurveyStatus>(),
		slug: varchar("slug", { length: 100 }).notNull().unique(),
		settings: text("settings").$type<SurveySettings>(), // JSON stored as text
		organizationId: integer("organization_id"), // For multi-tenancy
		ownerId: text("owner_id")
			.notNull()
			.references(() => user.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }),
		createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
		updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at")
			.defaultNow()
			.$onUpdate(() => new Date())
			.notNull(),
		publishedAt: timestamp("published_at"),
		closedAt: timestamp("closed_at"),
	},
	(table) => [
		index("survey_ownerId_idx").on(table.ownerId),
		index("survey_slug_idx").on(table.slug),
		index("survey_status_idx").on(table.status),
	],
);

export type SurveySettings = {
	anonymous: boolean;
	showProgressBar: boolean;
	brandingEnabled: boolean;
	primaryColor?: string;
	logoUrl?: string;
	thankYouMessage?: string;
	requireAuth: boolean;
};

export const surveyRelations = relations(survey, ({ one, many }) => ({
	owner: one(user, {
		fields: [survey.ownerId],
		references: [user.id],
	}),
	questions: many(/* question */),
	responses: many(/* response */),
}));
```

