### 4. Error Handling Pattern

Based on the existing codebase, errors should be thrown as standard JavaScript errors. For oRPC, we can use `ORPCError` for structured error handling:

```typescript
// Example of error handling pattern
import { ORPCError } from "@orpc/server";

// In handlers, throw ORPCError for structured errors
if (!result) {
	throw new ORPCError("NOT_FOUND", {
		message: "Survey not found",
	});
}

if (existing.ownerId !== context.session.user.id) {
	throw new ORPCError("FORBIDDEN", {
		message: "Access denied",
	});
}
```

